\description{
Every field-goal and free-throw attempt of a game (2016-17 onward) with its court position.

One row per attempt. Two coordinate systems share \code{pos_x} / \code{pos_y}, told apart by \code{coord_system}: \code{mm}
(match ids from 2020-21) is millimetres from the centre of the attacked basket, every shot mirrored to one
basket, \code{pos_x} towards midcourt and \code{pos_y} across the court (negative = the shooter's left); \code{x_basket_m}
/ \code{y_basket_m} are those in metres. \code{grid} (up to 2019-20) is a 0-100 percent grid over the full court, NOT
mirrored (teams switch ends at half time), and has no basket-relative metres (null). Free throws are (0, 0)
with a null \code{zone}; legacy zones are unreliable. The inference of units and origin is the refs' (arc and
sideline fit), not documented by ACB. \code{player_name} comes from the game's shooter list.

Endpoint: \verb{GET https://api2.acb.com/api/matchdata/MatchShots/match-shots}
}
